"
I am the root of the opaque handle classes generated by pharo-cig for libphuck.

I wrap a pointer to a C object owned by the shim (for example _phuck_t_). I carry no Pharo state: my instances are only valid while the C object is alive, and become null after an image restart.

My subclasses get their FFI library from LibTPhuck and their C type names from PhuckTypedef.

Generated code: do not add behaviour here, it is lost on regeneration..
"
Class {
	#name : 'PhuckBaseObject',
	#superclass : 'FFIOpaqueObject',
	#traits : 'LibTPhuck',
	#classTraits : 'LibTPhuck classTrait',
	#pools : [
		'PhuckTypedef'
	],
	#category : 'PhuckFFI-Core',
	#package : 'PhuckFFI',
	#tag : 'Core'
}
